<title>USA: Schroder Asian Growth may go open-ended.</title>
<headline>Schroder Asian Growth may go open-ended.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schroder Asian Growth Fund Inc said Wednesday that its board will recommend to stockholders that the fund be converted into an open-end structure.</p>
<p>The fund issued a statement saying it scheduled a special stockholders meeting on September 17 to vote on the open-ending proposal.</p>
<p>The fund said its investment objective will remain unchanged.</p>
<p>The fund, with assets of about $221 million, invests primarily in equity securities of Asian companies.</p>
</text>
